          "why": "r2.1 (verifier: the sheet's 'head_no_jaw' cell is a whole head with a painted lower jaw, so stacking pieces/jaw gave two jaws and two chins): derived from head_open_smile without a paid call. jaw_polygon (piece pixels, read by eye on a 3x gridded zoom) covers the lower lip line under the mouth, the chin and the head outline under it, from just inside the mouth's left corner (the corner and the lip line beside the cheek stay) to the head's right outline under the nose; the dark mouth interior is kept (tongue repainted with the interior colour) and the cut through the fur is closed with the head's own outline ink",
